    "name_suffix": "_2026",
    "long_instructions": "# Design Your Card\r\n\r\nYou are designing the layout for a single movie card. Before writing any code, you need to decide which fields belong on the card, where they go, and what happens when data is missing.\r\n\r\n## Steps\r\n1. **Review the movie data:** Look at the Example Object and the data plan. Notice the field names, their types, and which ones might be null.\r\n2. **Design your card layout:** In the Card View, arrange the fields from the data plan where you think they belong on the card. Not every field needs to appear — make intentional choices about what a user actually needs to see.\r\n3. **Plan your fallbacks:** For any field that might be null, add a note in the Card View with your fallback plan — what should the card show instead?\r\n4. **Save your work to your Backpack:** You'll need your data plan and card layout in the next level. "
  },
